  "verified_outcomes": [
    "One shared complete camera/FOV across entries, projects, an empty project, responsive remount, reload, fresh browser and actual API process restart, in both projection modes/layouts. Native projected landmarks and target-plane scale preserved at identical viewport.",
    "Actual first drawable surface fits once with positive focus radius and nondefault pose; navigation while upload is held cancels that opportunity.",
    "Same-browser actual close recovers an unacknowledged pose including a last raw 1e-7 update injected before the App pagehide flush, with no next renderer frame.",
    "Late hydration preserves newer native touch/mouse navigation; conflicts never overwrite automatically, survive reload with original dirty base, and publish only on explicit Save.",
    "Recovery remains reachable at 320px with the nonmodal manager open, passes axe and retains focused action while real PUT acknowledgement is held.",
    "Legacy scene wire fields omit FOV; applying a scene retains current FOV, while later navigation supersedes its held response. Native sub-epsilon update with matrixChanged=false persists and reloads exactly.",
    "Wire-valid but viewport-unrenderable saved poses report recoverable display failure, retaining startup, native geometry and explicit Fit.",
    "Independent API CAS insert/update races, stale identical rejection, exact no-op, all-old-table/history/Redo/timestamp invariance, archive exclusion, populated/empty migration round trips and artifact byte preservation pass."
  ],
  "corrections": [
    "Actual drawable geometry is separate from canonical target references; counting a Fit request alone did not prove fitting.",
    "Public cached canvas spheres can remain stale with manual resets; current render-object spheres and native BoundaryHelper98 now own clipping/Fit.",
    "Exact per-canvas native observation and guarded final capture close sub-epsilon publication and closure/replacement gaps; transform lock restores silently.",
    "Typed lazy restoration failures preserve usable startup and prevent fallback autosaves. Failed scene intent retires by generation/binding.",
    "Test setup now waits for actual drawability and accepted camera, and closes overlay controls before sending real canvas gestures."
  ],
  "diagnostic_limits": [
    "Earlier native1 first-fit counts were insufficient evidence; its default-camera result led to strengthened assertions and is not reused as final qualification.",
    "Native2 exposed stale provider bounds; native3 was interrupted by Vite dependency optimization reload after a new import. Subsequent source-frozen runs pass; no retries, skips or timing relaxation were introduced.",
    "An early reviewer inline probe awaited start() rather than hydration and was not a reliable hydrated reproduction. Corrected probe and new controlled regression tests establish final capture behavior."
  ],
